Aim: Hash basad file Comparison and Integrity verification

Tool used: Standard Linux/Unix tools for SHA-256 Hash generation.

Methodology

少 Baseline Generation

Ls Create a hash manifest of a clean set of system files.

2) Comparison

Modified a single byte within a configuration file and rehashed it to observe the avalanche effect

Verification

Used SHA-256 som-c to automatically check a list of files aganist a known good manifest

4) Collision Testing

↳ Discussed why MD5 is no longer sufficient for high-security environments as compared to SHA-256.

Result.

Successfully identified three files that were modified using the wiping utility

2) Demonstrated that hashing can detect even a 1-bit change in a 1GB file
